{%- comment -%}
  The site's one button.

  Extracted because the primary button's class string had been retyped in three
  places (hero-carousel, product-purchase, new-arrivals) and the B2B pages need
  it in eight more. A 400-character class list copied twelve times is a design
  token that drifts: the first divergence is a hover colour nobody notices, and
  after that the buttons on two pages are simply different buttons.

  Four variants, and the two `invert` ones exist because the B2B hero and the
  footer are espresso grounds. `secondary` on espresso reads as a disabled
  control — its `text-brand` is rgb(114,94,76) on rgb(30,26,22) — which is the
  same trap footer.liquid documents for its link colour.

  RENDERS EITHER ELEMENT. With `href` it is an `<a>`; without, a `<button>`.
  That matters for the cart and the quote form, where the control is a real
  submit, and for the hero, where it is navigation. A `<button>` that navigates
  and an `<a>` that submits are both wrong and both look like this.

  THE DISABLED LISTS ARE WRITTEN OUT TWICE ON PURPOSE, once bare for the anchor
  branch and once `disabled:`-prefixed for the button branch. Composing the
  second from the first — `off_classes | replace: ' ', ' disabled:'` — reads
  better and does not work: theme-src/theme.css scans these files as TEXT
  (`@source "../theme/snippets/*.liquid"`), so a class name that only exists
  after Liquid has run is a class name Tailwind never generates. Every utility
  in this file has to be literal here. That is the rule for the whole theme, and
  it is the one that fails silently.

  `aria-disabled` rather than `disabled` on the anchor branch: an anchor has no
  disabled state, and hiding it would remove the only clue about why the action
  is unavailable. The classes are applied directly there because `disabled:`
  variants do not match an attribute they cannot see.

  Accepts:
    label    - visible text
    href     - renders an <a>; omit for a <button>
    variant  - 'primary' (default) | 'secondary' | 'invert' | 'invert-outline'
    icon     - a mark from snippets/icon.liquid, drawn after the label
    type     - <button> type, default 'submit'
    name, value - <button> name and value, for a form with two submits
    form_id  - id of a form elsewhere in the document, for a button outside it
    disabled - unavailable; also drops the press
    class    - extra classes on the control
    attrs    - raw extra attributes, emitted verbatim
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign btn_variant = variant | default: 'primary'
  assign btn_type = type | default: 'submit'

  assign base = 'inline-flex min-h-13 items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-sm border px-11 text-caption uppercase tracking-[0.22em] transition-[background-color,color,border-color,transform] duration-(--duration-base) ease-out'

  case btn_variant
    when 'secondary'
      assign tone_classes = 'border-ink-subtle bg-transparent text-brand hover:border-brand hover:bg-brand hover:text-on-brand'
      assign off_classes = 'border-inert-border bg-inert text-on-inert'
      assign off_variants = 'disabled:border-inert-border disabled:bg-inert disabled:text-on-inert'
    when 'invert'
      assign tone_classes = 'border-surface bg-surface text-brand hover:border-canvas hover:bg-canvas'
      assign off_classes = 'border-ink-invert-muted bg-transparent text-ink-invert-muted'
      assign off_variants = 'disabled:border-ink-invert-muted disabled:bg-transparent disabled:text-ink-invert-muted'
    when 'invert-outline'
      assign tone_classes = 'border-ink-invert-muted bg-transparent text-ink-invert hover:border-ink-invert hover:bg-surface hover:text-brand'
      assign off_classes = 'border-ink-invert-muted bg-transparent text-ink-invert-muted'
      assign off_variants = 'disabled:border-ink-invert-muted disabled:bg-transparent disabled:text-ink-invert-muted'
    else
      assign tone_classes = 'border-brand bg-brand text-on-brand hover:border-brand-hover hover:bg-brand-hover'
      assign off_classes = 'border-disabled-border bg-disabled text-on-disabled'
      assign off_variants = 'disabled:border-disabled-border disabled:bg-disabled disabled:text-on-disabled'
  endcase
-%}

{%- if href != blank and disabled != true -%}
  <a
    href="{{ href }}"
    class="{{ base }} cursor-pointer active:translate-y-px {{ tone_classes }} {{ class }}"
    {{ attrs }}
  >{{ label }}{% if icon != blank %}{% render 'icon', icon: icon, class: 'size-5' %}{% endif %}</a>

{%- elsif href != blank -%}
  <span
    aria-disabled="true"
    class="{{ base }} cursor-not-allowed {{ off_classes }} {{ class }}"
    {{ attrs }}
  >{{ label }}{% if icon != blank %}{% render 'icon', icon: icon, class: 'size-5' %}{% endif %}</span>

{%- else -%}
  <button
    type="{{ btn_type }}"
    {% if name != blank %}name="{{ name }}"{% endif %}
    {% if value != blank %}value="{{ value }}"{% endif %}
    {% if form_id != blank %}form="{{ form_id }}"{% endif %}
    {% if disabled %}disabled{% endif %}
    class="{{ base }} cursor-pointer active:translate-y-px {{ tone_classes }} disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:translate-y-0 {{ off_variants }} {{ class }}"
    {{ attrs }}
  >{{ label }}{% if icon != blank %}{% render 'icon', icon: icon, class: 'size-5' %}{% endif %}</button>
{%- endif -%}
